from pathlib import Path
import json
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
C=json.loads((B/'courses-part1.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
def add(title,focus,source,test,symbol,model,before,after,example,concept,flow,exercises,answers):
 C.append(dict(title=title,focus=focus,source=source,test=test,symbol=symbol,model=model,before=before,after=after,example=example,concept=concept,flow=flow.split('|'),exercises=exercises,answers=answers))
add('Pantry Inventory: expiration versus stock','independent predicates, calendar rules and validation','app.js','test/expiration.test.cjs','getVisibleItems',
 'Quantity, minimum and expiration are separate fields. Low means quantity <= minimum. Expired means the YYYY-MM-DD label is earlier than local today.',
 'Fresh really meant above the stock threshold, so an expired item could appear fresh. Some invalid numeric values passed validation.',
 'Rows show stock and expiration independently. Expired filtering is available, and the in-stock/nonexpired view excludes expired items. New quantities must be finite and nonnegative, dates must be real, and returning to the tab refreshes date-based status.',
 'On September 8, an item expiring September 7 with quantity five and minimum one is Stock OK and Expired. An item expiring today with quantity one and minimum one is Low stock and not expired. Only a future sufficiently stocked item matches the combined view.',
 'A single status can hide independent dimensions. Compute low and expired separately and compose them for each view. Equality at the stock threshold is intentional: stock equal to minimum is already low. Equality at the date boundary has a different rule: this app treats the labeled date as valid through that day. Valid ISO labels sort chronologically, so string comparison is useful only after date validation. Reading local year, month and day avoids a UTC conversion that could shift the calendar label. This is an inventory software rule, not food-safety guidance. Visibility refresh does not schedule an exact update at midnight in a continuously visible tab. Existing malformed storage is not automatically migrated.',
 'Read local today|Evaluate low and expired separately|Compose status and search predicates|Render both conditions|Validate new numbers and dates|Refresh derived status when the tab returns',
 ['Add an expiring-within-seven-days view.','Add an expired count beside low stock.','Test leap-day and midnight boundaries.','Schedule a local-midnight refresh.'],
 ['Choose inclusive boundaries and build them with calendar addition; test today and the seventh day.','Count each predicate independently; an item may contribute to both.','Use fixed local dates around February 29 and avoid toISOString when deriving expected local labels.','Compute next local midnight with calendar setters, clear/reschedule the timer and avoid a fixed 24-hour assumption.'])
add('Snippet Vault: storage and clipboard failure','ES modules, normalization and rejected promises','src/store.js','test/store.test.js','saveSnippet',
 'The store owns snippets, main.js owns forms and views, and dom.js owns rendering/clipboard work. Tags retain their first display spelling while deduplicating lowercase comparison keys.',
 'The store mutated before writing, duplicate tag variants accumulated, and rejected clipboard promises could escape without feedback.',
 'Create, edit and delete publish only after persistence succeeds. Tags deduplicate case-insensitively, missing edit ids and blank content are rejected, and clipboard denial returns false so the UI can explain failure.',
 'Tags Utility,utility, EVENTS,events become Utility and EVENTS. A failed title-edit write leaves saved and in-memory titles unchanged. Clipboard rejection resolves false instead of producing an unhandled rejection.',
 'A useful module boundary owns a coherent responsibility. The store decides when data changes; rendering should not guess whether storage succeeded. Construct the candidate, write it and only then assign the module variable. If serialization or storage throws, assignment is skipped and the UI preserves the form. A Set of comparison keys removes duplicate tags while the first original spelling remains visible. Feature detection for navigator.clipboard is not permission: writeText may still reject, so the helper handles the asynchronous failure. Tests import actual ES modules under a fresh module identity for each fixture. Read methods still return object references; this change does not claim deep immutability against callers mutating those objects themselves.',
 'Collect form values|Normalize candidate fields and tags|Reject blank content or missing edit ids|Commit before publishing|Retain the form after rejection|Handle clipboard permission failure',
 ['Return defensive read copies.','Add a normalized tag filter.','Test clipboard absence and denial separately.','Add a validated versioned import/export.'],
 ['Copy records and tag arrays and test attempted mutation through a returned value.','Compare normalized tags while keeping display spelling; compose with existing filters.','Provide one fixture without the API and one whose promise rejects; neither should claim a successful copy.','Validate the entire envelope and all records before one commit, keeping ids and old state on failure.'])
add('Room Booking: editable reservations and time boundaries','half-open intervals, database constraints and timezones','server/src/validation.ts','test/booking.test.ts','parseBooking',
 'Bookings link a room UUID to a title, bookedBy label and two instants. PostgreSQL stores timestamptz and enforces room-specific nonoverlap using a GiST exclusion constraint.',
 'The UI could not edit although PUT existed. Runtime checks accepted malformed types or ambiguous timestamps, and local slot defaults mishandled midnight rollover.',
 'The UI edits existing ids and converts local input to explicit instants. The API validates ids, bounded text, real timestamps and forward windows. Day views send browser-local boundaries; a legacy date query explicitly means a UTC day. Database overlap enforcement is verified under concurrency and failed edits.',
 'Two requests for one room from 10:00 to 11:00 UTC yield one 201 and one 409. An adjacent 11:00-to-12:00 slot succeeds. Extending the first to 11:30 fails and preserves its old end. Renaming preserves its id. A query window ending at 11:00 excludes the adjacent slot.',
 'Half-open intervals include their start and exclude their end, so adjacent meetings can share a boundary. A check-then-insert in application code has a race; the database constraint is the final arbiter. A failed UPDATE preserves the previous row. datetime-local has no timezone, so the browser converts it to an ISO instant before submission. A local day is represented by two independently computed midnights, which can be 23 or 25 hours apart. The explicit legacy UTC-day policy avoids depending on a database session timezone. bookedBy is a human label, not authentication: this demo does not enforce ownership. Runtime validation gives helpful errors, while the constraint protects integrity even for competing writes. An overlap test and a failed-update test prove different postconditions.',
 'Load an existing booking into the editor|Convert local inputs to ISO instants|Validate UUIDs, text and time range|Let the database arbitrate overlap|Retain the editor on conflict|Refresh the schedule after an identity-preserving update',
 ['Add version-based stale-edit detection.','Display full dates across midnight.','Verify 23-hour and 25-hour day windows.','Add authenticated ownership.'],
 ['Condition the update on an expected version; the overlap constraint cannot detect lost edits.','Include dates when local start/end days differ, with accessible full timestamps.','Construct local midnight and next midnight in a fixed timezone and assert the UTC instants sent.','Use a verified caller identity and stored owner id at each access boundary, keeping bookedBy as separate display text.'])
add('Notes API: actual content search','PostgreSQL text search, runtime validation and stale responses','server/src/models/model.js','server/test/search.test.cjs','listRecords',
 'Notes have title, body, folder, status and JSON tags. Search indexes the meaning of title/body; folder/status are independent exact filters, and internal ids/timestamps do not participate.',
 'The API cast a whole row to text, and the UI searched serialized JSON locally. Internal metadata could match a document query. Payload field types were not enforced.',
 'English to_tsvector/plainto_tsquery search uses bound parameters over title/body. The UI debounces requests and ignores older responses. Payloads and filters are bounded, tags serialize correctly to JSON, and partial edits retain omitted fields.',
 'Running notes matches search run through stemming. A note whose folder is HiddenKeyword does not match that content query. Invalid tags are rejected before writing. Updating only body retains title/id and makes its new words searchable.',
 'Language-aware search is not substring matching. English stemming relates run and running, and stop words may disappear. plainto_tsquery treats input as plain terms rather than exposing operator syntax. Binding the parameter separates query structure from user values. Choosing only title/body makes the searched domain explicit. The current small app computes its vector in the query; it does not yet add a GIN index or relevance ranking. Debouncing reduces calls but does not stop an old slow response arriving last. A request version guards publication of results, errors and loading state. That version coordinates the UI and is not a database record version. Explicitly JSON-encoding tags avoids the driver interpreting a JavaScript array as a PostgreSQL array.',
 'Debounce a search change|Validate the text filters|Construct a content vector and bound query|Run the PostgreSQL search|Publish only the newest request version|Show searching or the matching count',
 ['Add a vector/index migration.','Rank by relevance with stable ties.','Test slow-old versus fast-new responses.','Design multilingual search.'],
 ['Generate or backfill the same configured vector, verify behavior equivalence and then measure a larger fixture.','Reuse the tsquery for rank and filtering; break ties by a documented stable field.','Delay the first stub response, return the second and prove the second remains visible after both finish.','Decide whether language belongs to each note or the workspace, migrate deliberately and test language-specific stemming.'])
add('Bookmark Manager: validated links and metadata','runtime schemas, outbound policy and controlled network tests','server/src/services/metadata.ts','server/test/metadata.test.ts','fetchMetadata',
 'Bookmarks store title, URL, collection, status and JSON tags. Saving a URL never fetches it. Explicit metadata preview proposes a title and URL without saving a bookmark.',
 'The scaffold copied fields without substantive runtime validation and lacked a metadata boundary. Emitted ESM paths also needed correction for a normal Node start.',
 'Zod validates create and partial updates. Metadata accepts configured exact HTTPS hosts on port 443, validates public IPv4 DNS answers, pins the connection, rejects redirects, and bounds headers/body/time. The UI applies a proposed title only if its URL still matches the request.',
 'A controlled host returns title A &amp; B, yielding A & B. A redirect to loopback is rejected without contacting its target. Private DNS, unlisted hosts, oversized bodies and timeouts fail. DNS finishing after timeout cannot start a transfer. A javascript: URL is rejected before insertion.',
 'Saving URL text and fetching it are distinct permission boundaries. The empty-by-default BOOKMARK_METADATA_HOSTS allowlist prevents ambient requests during ordinary saves. An allowed name can still resolve to a private address: validate its DNS answers, then pin a checked address into the real connection lookup while retaining the hostname for TLS verification. Otherwise a second DNS decision could differ from the checked result. Rejecting every redirect avoids a new unchecked target. One deadline covers DNS and response work, and delayed DNS checks the abort state before starting transport. The conservative policy supports only public IPv4 HTTPS and uncompressed HTML; it is not a universal website scraper. Tests substitute the connection factory to reach a local stub while retaining real response-status, size and timeout handling. No external website was contacted for verification.',
 'Explicitly request a page title|Validate the URL and configured host|Resolve and validate destination addresses|Pin one public address for bounded transfer|Parse only a successful bounded response|Apply the title only if the form URL is unchanged',
 ['Explain disabled metadata capability before requesting.','Improve bounded title entity decoding.','Test mixed DNS answers and forbidden ports.','Design safe redirect support.'],
 ['Expose a capability flag without secrets and retain manual entry in every state.','Use a parser that neither executes scripts nor fetches resources; bound input first and render output as text.','Return public and private answers together and assert no transfer. Test non-443 ports and credentials separately.','Limit hops, revalidate and pin every target, retain one deadline/byte budget and forward no credentials. Keep redirects rejected until those cases are verified.'])
for n,c in enumerate(C,11):
 c['testcmd']='npm test' if n<=18 else 'cd server\nnpm test'
 if n in [11,12,13,15,16]:c['setup']='Open index.html in a browser. From this project folder run `npm install`, then `npm test` with Node 22 or a compatible later version for the DOM tests.'
 elif n==17:c['setup']='Serve the project over HTTP with `python -m http.server 8000`, then open http://localhost:8000. ES modules cannot be opened through file://. Run `npm test` with Node 22 for the module checks.'
 elif n==14:c['setup']='From the project root run `npm install`, `npm run dev`, `npm test`, and `npm run build` as needed. Vite serves client/ and the API defaults to port 4106. Normal startup creates server/data/notes.json if absent; tests use disposable temporary files. Run one port-4106 project at a time.'
 elif n==18:c['setup']='Install dependencies at the project root. Configure DATABASE_URL for a new empty development database. The existing db:setup script resets its tables, so use it only for that disposable setup. Run `npm run dev`, `npm run build` and `npm run typecheck` at the root. Tests use a separate astra_test_* database and run with `npm test` at the root.'
 else:c['setup']='Install dependencies in server and client separately. Follow the root README and .env.example for your development database. Run API scripts from server and frontend scripts from client. Tests require ASTRA_TEST_DATABASE_URL pointing at a dedicated astra_test_* database; they create an isolated schema rather than use development records.'
 if n==20:c['setup']+=' Metadata is disabled until BOOKMARK_METADATA_HOSTS contains exact HTTPS hostnames. Manual bookmark creation needs no metadata configuration. Verification used only a controlled local stub.'
 c['dbguide']=''
 if n>=18:c['dbguide']='''## Database test setup

Create a dedicated PostgreSQL database such as astra_test_learning. Set your own test credentials in PowerShell:

```powershell
$env:ASTRA_TEST_DATABASE_URL = 'postgres://YOUR_TEST_USER:YOUR_TEST_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/astra_test_learning'
```

Tests reject differently named databases. The user must be allowed to create schemas. Each run creates and drops only its unique schema. Room Booking additionally enables btree_gist and pgcrypto in this dedicated test database; it does not run the scaffold's DROP TABLE statements against a fallback namespace. Run npm test from the Room Booking root or the Notes/Bookmark server folder. Interrupted runs can leave owned schemas; inspect the dedicated database before cleaning them up. Configuration must precede importing the app's database module.
'''
